WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.867
Polymorphism.

2
00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:05.463
Different classes can answer the same call in their own way.

3
00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:07.167
That's what makes plugins easy.

4
00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:12.467
Polymorphism means different classes answer the same method call.

5
00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:14.733
Python's flavor is duck typing.

6
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:19.433
The calling code cares that dot run exists, not which class it belongs to.

7
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:22.300
Picture one call fanning out.

8
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.400
The same call, tool dot run, goes to whichever object happens to receive it.

9
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.833
The asteroid tool answers with near Earth asteroids.

10
00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:36.064
The solar flare tool answers with flares, and the events tool with natural events.

11
00:00:36.064 --> 00:00:37.267
Each in its own way.

12
00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.767
Compare the two styles.

13
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:44.100
Checking types means an extra branch every time you add a class.

14
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.564
Duck typing just calls the method.

15
00:00:46.564 --> 00:00:49.300
A new class needs no changes anywhere else.

16
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.800
Here it is in Python.

17
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.933
Two unrelated classes, each with a run method.

18
00:00:55.233 --> 00:00:58.100
One loop calls run on each, with no type checks.

19
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.800
And each object responds in its own way.

20
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.633
This is how plugin architectures stay simple.

21
00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:09.567
The agent's execution loop just calls run on whatever tools are registered.

22
00:01:09.867 --> 00:01:14.167
To add the Exoplanet Archive, you write one new class with a run method.

23
00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:18.167
The loop, the retry wrapper, and the tracing all work unchanged.

24
00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:20.127
Let's recap.

25
00:01:20.127 --> 00:01:23.800
Polymorphism is different classes answering the same call.

26
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.967
Duck typing means no type checks, no interface declarations.

27
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.433
New features need just one new class.

28
00:01:30.733 --> 00:01:34.004
And typing dot Protocol gives it a static spine.

29
00:01:34.004 --> 00:01:35.367
Next up: decorators.
